      "description": "Watch 1. FC Heidenheim vs VfL Osnabrück highlights and goals from 2. Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. The 2. Bundesliga encounter between 1. FC Heidenheim and VfL Osnabrück promised a tactical battle of high stakes, drawing fans into an atmosphere thick with anticipation. Both sides took to the pitch looking to establish dominance in a match that would eventually unfold into a classic goal-fest. An Explosive First-Half Exchange On August 9, 2026 , the match ignited early as the hosts found their rhythm within the first ten minutes. Budu Zivzivadze opened the scoring for 1. FC Heidenheim in the 10th minute, clinical in his finish after being set up by Marcel Costly . The lead, however, was temporary. VfL Osnabrück fought back with determination, and by the 23rd minute, Niklas Wiemann had leveled the score following a precise assist from Konrad Faber . The see-saw nature of the contest continued as Marcel Costly turned from provider to goalscorer in the 29th minute, restoring the lead for the home side. Yet, the visitors remained undeterred. David Kopacz struck back in the 34th minute, once again assisted by Konrad Faber , to make it 2-2. The drama of the first half reached its peak in stoppage time when Jan Schoeppner found the net in the 45+2 minute, thanks to a delivery from Jonas Foehrenbach , sending Heidenheim into the locker room with a slim advantage. Late Security and Penalty Drama The second half saw a shift in intensity as tactical substitutions and yellow cards, including one for Oualid Mhamdi , slowed the initial frantic pace. As the clock wound down, it appeared the points were secured in the 89th minute when Marvin Pieringer extended the lead to 4-2, capitalizing on another Marcel Costly assist. However, VfL Osnabrück refused to go quietly. In the second minute of added time, Robin Meissner converted a penalty to bring the score to 4-3, ensuring a nervous final few moments for the home crowd. Despite the late pressure during the nine minutes of injury time, Heidenheim held firm until the final whistle, concluding a breathtaking encounter that showcased the very best of German football's second tier."
